    {
      "role": "calculations",
      "heading": "Six operating-economics modules",
      "text": "Income reconciliation derives gross profit and operating income, then checks the reported result. Margins distinguish gross and operating economics. Product mix reconciles the two product franchises. Manufacturing costs reconcile wafer, package/test and logistics expense. Operating investment separates engineering from commercial and administrative expense. Sequential actuals compare revenue, income and point-in-time headcount without treating the latter as a quarterly flow.",
